     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Daily total:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The FDA-labeled maximum for immediate-release metformin is 2,550 mg/day, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. This order is about twice the maximum.\n- **Single dose:** 1700 mg is well above the usual maximum of about 1,000 mg per dose. That much at once raises the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals:** 2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release.\n- **1000 mg twice daily with meals:** 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg** at a different frequency.\n- **1700 mg/day total,** for example 850 mg twice daily.\n\nIf you do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that it's intentional and give the clinical rationale. I'll then enter it with a note documenting that. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
